<title>USA: IFC launches $50 mln 5-year-note, targetting Japan.</title>
<headline>IFC launches $50 mln 5-year-note, targetting Japan.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The International Finance Corp, an affiliate of the World Bank, said Tuesday it launched a $50 million five-year fixed rate note targeted to the Japanese market.</p>
<p>It said the note, issued under the IFC's Euro Medium Term Note program, carries a semi-annual coupon of 5.81 percent per annum and an issue price of 100 percent.</p>
<p>The joint-lead managers are SBC Warburg and Toyo Securities Ltd.</p>
<p>The IFC promotes the private sector in developing countries.</p>
</text>
